        "params": {
          "text": "**FN02 \u2014 Three ways to excite a system**  \n**1 Predict \u2192 2 Run \u2192 3 Inspect \u2192 4 Change one thing.** Run **2 s at 10 Hz**, then open Scope.  \nSame rule: `y[n]=u[n]+0.5 y[n\u22121]`. Inputs begin at n=5 (Scope time 0.6 s).  \nBefore n=5 only natural response remains. At n=5 both forced responses start at 1 V.  \nTry: select step, press F4, change final_value 1 to 2; rerun. Which curve changes?  \n[Open FN02 student lab](qrc:/s7studio/help/education/labs/FN02-natural-forced/README.md) \u00b7 [MIT difference equations](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/6-003-signals-and-systems-fall-2011/resources/mit6_003f11_chap1/) \u00b7 [MIT block diagrams](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/6-003-signals-and-systems-fall-2011/resources/mit6_003f11_chap3/)",
